It's near perfect;
The gameplay is fun and addictive (especially driving), there's a huge amount of things to do (like flying a plane, eating and getting fat, changing your clothes and your hairstyle, fighting over gang territories, or robbing a house.) the map is enormous and contains not just cities, but also countryside, desert, mountains, lakes, and more, and the game is so big there are even myths for it. It also runs quite well on old computers.
However, it's not perfect, because on ocassions you're going to be extremely frustrated when playing some of the missions and the spawn system can be really annoying at times (for example - when driving, sometimes when you look in a different direction a car spawns right in front of you).

